diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 1a879e0..b96a378 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -28,6 +28,8 @@ Customers register at `POST /api/v1/registrations`, then use the standard verifi
 
 Staff can set each ticket's `priority` to `normal` (the default) or `high`. Staff ticket responses include priority, while customer request responses do not. Staff can combine `status`, `assignee_id`, `group_id`, `requester_id`, `priority`, and `q` filters on `/api/v1/tickets`; `assignee_id=unassigned` selects tickets without an assignee. `q` is a case-insensitive literal search of subjects and public comments. Customer request lists support only the `status` filter.
 
+Staff can merge duplicate tickets for the same customer with `POST /api/v1/tickets/:id/merge` and a JSON `merge.target_id`. The source becomes `closed` and both ticket views expose `merged_into_id`, including `null` for unmerged tickets; `status=closed` filters are supported in both staff and customer lists. Merge notes are private by default and may be customized independently with `source_comment` and `target_comment` objects containing `body` and `public`. Merges never move comments or send email for their notes, and closed tickets remain readable but reject edits and inbound email replies.
+
 Admins manage staff invitations through `/api/v1/invitations`, including list/show, `POST /api/v1/invitations/:id/resend`, and `DELETE /api/v1/invitations/:id`. Invitations expire after seven days. The frontend previews a token with `POST /invitation_previews` (also available at `/api/v1/invitation_previews`) and accepts it at `POST /api/v1/invitation_acceptances`. Accepted staff are verified immediately.
 
 Admins list and inspect users at `/api/v1/users` and update roles or suspension at `/api/v1/users/:id`. User lists can filter by `role` and `suspended`. `GET /api/v1/staff` returns all active admin and agent choices for ticket assignment. Suspending a user revokes their sessions and clears their ticket assignments; the last active admin cannot be suspended or demoted.
